From 126d9a35b53e0c3694a17c3161e0fc6fed99f3f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:42:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: pin run-list-error continue, non-I/O
 propagation and the in-progress page size in the CI-progress pool scan

Post-merge check t_01a1d5e5c01ace56 of #2380/#2397 found three exact-anchor
mutants of `_recent_job_on` that the suite did not kill (74 passed each).
Tests only; no production change.

- A4: `continue` -> `break` after an unreadable run list. New
  test_unreadable_in_progress_run_list_does_not_skip_the_completed_runs
  [match/no-match]: the in-progress list raises HTTP 502, the completed list
  holds a recent run whose job matches (BUSY, remembered) or does not
  (NOT_STARTING, not remembered).
- A6: dropping `if not isinstance(exc, unreadable): raise exc` in batch().
  New test_unexpected_job_read_error_propagates_out_of_the_scan
  [KeyError/TypeError]: ci_run_progress catches no non-I/O error from the
  pool scan, so it propagates (to the sweep's own handler) and nothing is
  remembered.
- B2: in-progress per_page 100 -> 25. test_scan_lists_more_than_ten_in_progress_runs
  now lists IN_PROGRESS_RUNS_MAX runs with the match at the last index, so
  any page size below the cap fails (index 21 only caught <= 21).

RED/GREEN (scripts/run_tests.sh tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress.py):
  base+tests: 78 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped
  A4: 2 failed (the new run-list test, both params), 76 passed
  A6: 2 failed (the new propagation test, both params), 76 passed
  B2: 1 failed (test_scan_lists_more_than_ten_in_progress_runs), 77 passed
scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks, ok.

Card: t_01a1d5fa17bb4590
